# Fingerprints gitleaks should not report, in `commit:file:rule:line` form.
#
# Fingerprints rather than a path or rule allowlist on purpose. Suppressing `generic-api-key`
# across `crates/**` or turning it off for markdown would also suppress a real key committed
# to those paths tomorrow. Each line here waives exactly one finding in exactly one historical
# commit, so the scanner stays fully armed everywhere else.
#
# Both entries below are the `generic-api-key` heuristic matching prose *about* cryptography
# rather than any credential. Verified by reading the source lines:
#
#   * CHANGELOG.md:19 — the release note describing the HKDF-SHA-512 subkey namespace.
#   * aead.rs:1 — the module doc comment opening "Authenticated encryption:".
#
# The commit predates the rename, hence the old `keel-crypto` path. Rewriting history to
# change it would invalidate these fingerprints and every published commit hash, for a
# cosmetic gain.
b2a45dd522f94ee2b6158f1f554f40407a8de49a:CHANGELOG.md:generic-api-key:19
